      "title": "Cereal production Is 1.5x Higher Than In 1972",
      "hook": "By the 1970s, experts were warning the world would run out of food.",
      "says": [
        "In 1985, progression to secondary school (%) was 77.8; by 2017, 91.3—1.2 times higher.",
        "In 1972, cereal production was 1083.7 million metric tons; by 2024, 1644.1—1.5 times higher.",
        "China leads: 5.2; United States: 4.2; Australia: 3.6; Brazil: 2.4; Russia: 2.2 million square kilometers."
      ],
      "closing": "The famine everyone predicted never showed up.",
      "question": "Which surprised you most—school, grain, or land?"
    },
